SUMMARY:Name That Tune (The Very Best of 7 Decades) (October 24th)  
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nHello everyone\,\n\n
 How well do you know your music? Come join us for a fun day of Name That T
 une as we travel through seven decades of unforgettable songs!\nFrom old f
 avourites and classic hits to songs you may not have heard in years\, we
 ’ll put our musical memories to the test while enjoying a relaxed day of
  laughs\, drinks\, food and good company.\n\n\\*Please note that we are at
  The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of
  Lawrence and south of the 401). We are in the back dining area—come fin
 d us!\n\n\\*Joined by my other groups too :)\n\nEvent details below:\n\nSi
 ncerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n─────────
 ─────\nEVENT DETAILS\n**Name That Tune – The Very Best of 7 De
 cades!**\nThink you can recognize a song after hearing just a portion of i
 t? We’ll be playing music from seven decades and seeing who can name tho
 se tunes!\n\\*You will be in groups of 4 to 6 people (working as a team)\n
 • Music spanning seven decades\n• Classic hits and memorable favourite
 s from different eras\n• A fun mix of genres and musical styles\n• Tes
 t your music knowledge and memory\n• Play along individually or work tog
 ether with others\n• Meet new people and reconnect with familiar faces\n
 • Plenty of laughs\, food\, drinks and friendly competition\n• No musi
 cal expertise required—just come out and have fun!\nWhether you know eve
 ry song or can barely remember the title\, this is about enjoying some gre
 at music\, sharing memories and having a fun night with friends!\n──
 ────────────\nFRIENDLY REMINDERS\nEvent fee: $10 p
 er person for reserved seating and event organization.\nFood and drinks ar
 e purchased separately.\nPay the event fee in cash at the event or by e-tr
 ansfer in advance to:\n[steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemming11@
 gmail.com)\n\\*Great dinner menu and food specials provided\n\\*One bevera
 ge or appetizer minimum upon arrival to support the venue\n─────
 ─────────\nPARKING AND TRANSPORTATION\n\\*Lots of street
  parking on Avenue Road and free residential parking\nThe Pheasant: A Firk
 in Pub:\n[https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/](https://www.fi
 rkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/)\n\\*15–20 minute walk from Yonge & L
 awrence subway station—or simply take the bus or an Uber from the statio
 n.
