SUMMARY:Sunday Afternoon Movie Trivia and Great Memories! 
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nHello everyone\,\n\n
 Join us for a fun and relaxing Sunday afternoon celebrating some of the gr
 eatest movies ever made!\n\nWe'll revisit unforgettable movie scenes\, fam
 ous quotes\, memorable characters\, and classic films from across the deca
 des. Enjoy some friendly trivia\, laughter\, conversation\, and great memo
 ries while meeting new people.\n\nWhether you're a movie enthusiast or sim
 ply enjoy a little nostalgia\, everyone is welcome!\n\nPlease note that we
  are at The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks n
 orth of Lawrence and south of the 401). We are in the back dining area—c
 ome find us!\nJoined by my other groups too :)\n\nEvent details below:\n\n
 Sincerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\nSoul City Social Club\n\n
 ***\n\n## EVENT DETAILS\n\n**Event:** **Sunday Afternoon Movie Trivia and 
 Great Memories!**\n**Date:** Sunday\, November 8\, 2026\n**Arrival Time:**
  3:00 pm to 3:45 pm\n**Location:** The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub\n1999 Avenue
  Road\, Toronto\n**Hosted by:** Steve Flemming — Soul City Social Club\n
 **Age requirement:** 19+\n**Event fee:** $10 per person for reserved seati
 ng and event organization.\nFood and drinks are purchased separately.\n\n*
 **\n\n## FRIENDLY REMINDERS\n\n* Please mention Steve with Meetup when you
  arrive.\n* Pay the event fee in cash at the event or by e-transfer in adv
 ance to: [steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemming11@gmail.com)\n* 
 Great lunch and dinner menu and food specials available.\n* One beverage o
 r appetizer minimum upon arrival to support the venue.\n\n***\n\n## PARKIN
 G AND TRANSPORTATION\n\nFree street parking is available in the surroundin
 g residential neighbourhood.\n\nThe Pheasant is located on Avenue Road\, n
 orth of Lawrence Avenue and south of Highway 401.\n\nFor those taking publ
 ic transportation\, it's approximately a 15–20-minute walk from Yonge an
 d Lawrence.\n\nLooking forward to an enjoyable afternoon of movie trivia\,
  wonderful memories\, and good company!
